    "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/049.jpg\" alt=\"Daman (GRSIA) — the public homepage, &quot;Connecting Generations,&quot; with Individual and Corporate gates, live News Room and impact numbers\" width=\"1150\" height=\"2488\" loading=\"eager\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\">The <b>Daman</b> homepage — “Connecting Generations,” with separate\n          Individual and Corporate entry gates, a live News Room, impact numbers (175K pensioners, 108 investments, 122\n          partner offers) and the GRSIA mobile app, all under the same persistent <b>Sara</b> assistant that follows the\n          visitor through the rest of the platform.</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/050.jpg\" alt=\"Daman (GRSIA) — Frequently Asked Questions, organised into nine categories from General Questions to Extending Insurance Coverage, with the Sara virtual assistant\" width=\"1150\" height=\"1533\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\">Qatar's pension and social-insurance authority rebranded its public identity as <b>“Daman”</b>\n          (ضمان, “guarantee”) — a persistent virtual assistant, <b>Sara</b>, sits on every\n          page shown here, including this FAQ system, which sorts pension and retirement regulation into nine navigable\n          categories instead of one long list.</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-pair\">\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/051.jpg\" alt=\"Daman Media Center — List of News, filterable by year and month, with search\" width=\"600\" height=\"1169\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/052.jpg\" alt=\"Daman Media Center — List of Albums, part of the Multimedia section\" width=\"600\" height=\"936\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\">The Media Center consolidates five different content types — Multimedia, News,\n          Articles, Publications and Archive — behind one shared template: the same hero, tab switcher, search and\n          filterable grid, so a visitor never has to relearn the pattern moving between them.</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-pair\">\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/053.jpg\" alt=\"Daman Media Center — an individual news article page with a Key Points list, Article Summary and Other News\" width=\"600\" height=\"1106\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/054.jpg\" alt=\"Daman Media Center — Daman's Magazine detail page with a table of contents and edition selector\" width=\"600\" height=\"1074\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\">The same “grid out, detail in” pattern reused for a news article (left, with a\n          Key Points list and an Article Summary for a dense regulatory topic) and a full magazine edition (right, with its\n          own table of contents and a downloadable PDF).</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/055.jpg\" alt=\"El Safwa — Daman's retiree discounts marketplace, with category tiles, a filterable Discounts List and a Get Offer card for each partner\" width=\"1150\" height=\"3346\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\"><b>El Safwa</b> (الصفوة) — Daman's enhanced\n          retiree-benefits programme, offering exclusive partner discounts across categories from cafes to healthcare. It's\n          the most unusual piece of the system: a retail-style marketplace, with filters, sorting and pagination, carried by\n          the same government authority that runs pension calculations two clicks away.</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-pair\">\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/056.jpg\" alt=\"Daman Media Center — the full List of Magazines archive grid\" width=\"600\" height=\"1196\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n          <div class=\"cd-shot\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"assets/img/057.jpg\" alt=\"Daman — Let's Get in Touch contact page, with call, email, hours and social channels, a message form and an office map\" width=\"600\" height=\"653\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"cd-caption\">Left — the Archive behind every magazine edition. Right — Contact Us, with\n          four ways in (phone, email, service hours, social) alongside a structured message form and the office location on\n          a map, for the pensioners and staff who still need a human.</p>\n        <div class=\"cd-copy\">\n          <h4 class=\"lbl\">The Brief</h4>\n          <p>GRSIA administers pensions and social insurance for Qatar's retirees and workforce, and was rolling out a new\n            public identity, “Daman,” built on four pillars — trust, transparency, care and sustainability\n            — to make a historically bureaucratic authority feel approachable. A large share of its users are older\n            and less digitally native, so self-service content had to be legible without a branch visit or a phone call,\n            across a genuinely wide surface: FAQs spanning nine regulatory categories, a five-format Media Center, a\n            retiree-discounts programme, and every contact channel the authority offers. My scope covered the full UI and UX end-to-end across the whole system.</p>\n          <h4 class=\"lbl\">My Approach</h4>\n          <p>The real challenge was consistency across very different kinds of content without flattening any of them. For\n            the Media Center, I built one template — hero, tab switcher, search, filterable grid, detail view —\n            and reused it across Multimedia, News, Articles, Publications and Archive, so five separate content types read\n            as one system instead of five disconnected sections. For the FAQ, instead of one long scroll of questions, I\n            organised pension and retirement law into nine audience-shaped categories (Subscribers &amp; Employers,\n            Retirement Rights, Those Who Deserve It, Pensioner's Return to Work, and more) so a visitor narrows to their\n            situation before reading anything. El Safwa was the hardest balance: a discounts marketplace needed the\n            immediacy of a retail experience — category tiles, filters, a “Get Offer” card — while\n            still sitting credibly inside a government authority's visual identity, so I carried Daman's own palette,\n            typography and card language into it rather than borrowing an e-commerce template wholesale. And Sara, the\n            virtual assistant, runs as one persistent presence across every page shown here — FAQs, Media Center,\n            El Safwa, Contact — as a constant fallback for anyone who doesn't want to search or read.</p>\n          <h4 class=\"lbl\">Outcome</h4>\n          <p>A single, consistent system carrying Daman's rebrand across everything a pensioner, subscriber or employer\n            might come to the site for — regulatory self-service through a categorised FAQ, five content types under\n            one Media Center template, an unusually retail-feeling discounts programme in El Safwa, and a persistent\n            assistant and full contact system for anyone who still needs a person. Helping take a national pension\n            authority from a purely bureaucratic interface to “Daman” is one of the projects I'm proudest of.\n            </p>\n          \n        </div>"
